And there are only three.

06:08.260 --> 06:08.800
Just three?

06:08.980 --> 06:09.400
Just three.

06:09.400 --> 06:14.480
This is the primitive dynamical object of the entire theory called the relativistic scalar

06:14.480 --> 06:18.120
vector plenum, or the RSVP framework for short.

06:18.780 --> 06:19.260
RSVP.

06:19.460 --> 06:20.060
I like that.

06:20.300 --> 06:24.140
So mathematically, it is a field triple defined on a smooth manifold.

06:24.780 --> 06:28.440
Let's define those three ingredients because they sound abstract, but they are the entire

06:28.440 --> 06:29.800
basis for this universe.

06:29.940 --> 06:30.520
Let's do it.

06:30.520 --> 06:33.640
First, we have phi, representing scalar capacity.

06:34.280 --> 06:38.740
The paper describes it as a generalized energetic or organizational capacity.

06:38.860 --> 06:38.940
Right.

06:39.040 --> 06:39.740
It didn't have a direction.

06:39.940 --> 06:41.960
It's just a raw value at any given point.

06:42.040 --> 06:42.160
Okay.

06:42.880 --> 06:45.500
Second, we have V, which is vector transport.

06:45.800 --> 06:47.300
This is a directional field.

06:47.440 --> 06:49.220
It defines trajectories and flow.

06:49.220 --> 06:53.020
And finally, S, which stands for entropy density.

06:53.420 --> 06:59.380
And this is a measure of local uncertainty, fragmentation, or unresolved multiplicity.

06:59.380 --> 07:03.400
The absence of traditional physical properties here is what you should really focus on.

07:03.500 --> 07:03.600
Right.

07:03.660 --> 07:05.060
Because there's no mass parameter, right?

07:05.060 --> 07:05.640
No mass.

07:05.840 --> 07:07.380
There is no electric charge parameter.

07:07.520 --> 07:10.860
There isn't even a metric tensor telling things how spacetime is curved.

07:10.860 --> 07:13.460
It's literally just capacity, direction, and disorder.

07:13.680 --> 07:14.080
That's it.

07:14.680 --> 07:15.200
Okay.

07:15.420 --> 07:19.800
I want to try and visualize this because fields can be incredibly hard to picture.

